editor.nod_help.chg.extra=<h2>Esempi chg</h2><p><a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:chg"><code>chg</code></a> cambia l inizio del testo o un pattern. È utile per numeri telefonici, codici, prefissi e tabelle di rinumerazione.</p><div class="notice"><b>Struttura:</b> sinistra = cosa cercare, destra = nuova forma. Usa le virgolette per spazi, virgole o caratteri speciali.</div><details open><summary>Sostituire prefisso</summary><table><tr><th>Obiettivo</th><th>Regola</th><th>Esempio</th></tr><tr><td>Prefix</td><td><code>chg "01751","07051"</code></td><td><code>0175112345</code> -> <code>0705112345</code></td></tr><tr><td>Dash</td><td><code>chg "01751-","070-51"</code></td><td><code>01751-12345</code> -> <code>070-5112345</code></td></tr></table></details><details><summary>Pattern con x</summary><p>NOD 2.0: <code>x</code> cattura una cifra e la reinserisce a destra. Spazi e trattini a sinistra servono solo per leggere meglio.</p><pre>chg "0183x-xx xx","0183-x0 xx xx"</pre><p><code>01835-1234</code> -> <code>0183-501234</code>.</p></details><details><summary>Errori comuni</summary><ul><li>Metti le regole specifiche sopra quelle generiche.</li><li>Non dimenticare la virgola.</li><li>Usa <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:trans"><code>trans</code></a> per tradurre un valore completo.</li></ul></details>
editor.nod_help.math.extra=<h2>Math in breve</h2><p><a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:math"><code>math</code></a> calcola con <code>ans</code>. Nella prima riga <code>ans</code> è il valore inserito; nelle righe successive è il risultato precedente.</p><div class="notice"><b>Struttura:</b> scegli prima il tipo di calcolo e poi scrivi la syntax corretta. Per formule grandi usa parentesi o più righe <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:math"><code>math</code></a>.</div><div class="math-flow"><span class="math-pill">1. Operazioni di base</span><span class="math-pill">2. Funzioni e costanti</span><span class="math-pill">3. Formule complesse</span><span class="math-pill">4. Calcolo: diff, integrale, limite</span></div><details open><summary>Operazioni di base</summary><table><tr><th>Obiettivo</th><th>Syntax</th><th>Esempio</th></tr><tr><td>+</td><td><code>math ans + number</code></td><td><code>math ans + 32</code></td></tr><tr><td>-</td><td><code>math ans - number</code></td><td><code>math ans - 10</code></td></tr><tr><td>*</td><td><code>math ans * factor</code></td><td><code>math ans * 1.8</code></td></tr><tr><td>/</td><td><code>math ans / factor</code></td><td><code>math ans / 1.95583</code></td></tr></table><pre>Name Euro to cents&#13;&#10;input1 Euro&#13;&#10;input2 Cents&#13;&#10;format #.00&#13;&#10;math ans * 100&#13;&#10;end</pre></details><details><summary>Funzioni e costanti</summary><table><tr><th>Groep</th><th>Syntax</th><th>Nota</th></tr><tr><td>Power</td><td><code>math ans^2</code> or <code>math pow(ans,3)</code></td><td>Square, cube.</td></tr><tr><td>Root</td><td><code>math sqrt(ans)</code></td><td>Can be used inside formulas.</td></tr><tr><td>Pi/e</td><td><code>math pi * ans^2</code><br><code>math e^ans</code></td><td>Circle and exponential.</td></tr><tr><td>Degrees</td><td><code>math sind(ans)</code><br><code>math cosd(ans)</code></td><td>Use <code>sin/cos/tan</code> for radians.</td></tr></table></details><details><summary>Formule complesse</summary><p>Usa le parentesi quando l ordine è importante. Scrivi sempre la moltiplicazione con <code>*</code>.</p><pre>math sqrt(ans^2 + 25)&#13;&#10;math ((ans + 10) * 2) / 3&#13;&#10;math ans * (1 + 0.04)^5</pre><h3>Esempio: Pitagora</h3><div class="mathml-formula"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="inline"><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>5</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt></mrow></math></div><pre>Name Hypotenuse&#13;&#10;input1 Side a&#13;&#10;input2 Side c&#13;&#10;format #.00&#13;&#10;math sqrt(ans^2 + 25)&#13;&#10;end</pre><p>Qui <code>ans</code> è il lato <code>a</code>; l altro lato è fisso a <code>5</code>.</p></details><details><summary>Calcolo: diff, integrale, limite</summary><table><tr><th>Obiettivo</th><th>Syntax</th><th>Risultato</th></tr><tr><td>Derivative</td><td><code>math diff ans^2</code></td><td>Pendenza numerica.</td></tr><tr><td>Integral</td><td><code>math integral 0,1 ans^2</code></td><td>Area numerica da 0 a 1.</td></tr><tr><td>Limit</td><td><code>math limit 0 sin(ans)/ans</code></td><td>Approssimazione intorno a 0.</td></tr></table></details><h2>Errori comuni</h2><ul><li>Non dimenticare <code>ans</code>.</li><li>Usa <code>sind</code> per i gradi.</li><li>Usa <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:reverse"><code>reverse</code></a> per conversioni inverse complesse.</li></ul>
editor.nod_help.mode.extra=<h2>Quando usare mode?</h2><p><a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:mode"><code>mode</code></a> indica quale tipo di file NOD stai creando. Per un convertitore normale di solito non serve.</p><div class="notice"><b>Struttura:</b> usa <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:mode"><code>mode</code></a> solo per tipi speciali, come elaborazione dati o risoluzione di equazioni.</div><details open><summary>Modes</summary><table><tr><th>Mode</th><th>Quando</th><th>Comandi</th></tr><tr><td><code>mode calculator</code></td><td>Convertitore normale</td><td><a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:math"><code>math</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:trans"><code>trans</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:chg"><code>chg</code></a></td></tr><tr><td><code>mode data</code></td><td>Elaborazione dati</td><td><a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:table"><code>table</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:field"><code>field</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:output"><code>output</code></a></td></tr><tr><td><code>mode equation</code></td><td>Risolvere equazione</td><td><a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:given"><code>given</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:equation"><code>equation</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:solve"><code>solve</code></a></td></tr></table></details><details><summary>Esempio: converter</summary><pre>Name Celsius to Fahrenheit&#13;&#10;input1 Celsius&#13;&#10;input2 Fahrenheit&#13;&#10;format #.00&#13;&#10;math ans * 1.8&#13;&#10;math ans + 32&#13;&#10;end</pre></details><details><summary>Esempio: equation</summary><pre>Name Solve equation&#13;&#10;mode equation&#13;&#10;given y = 20&#13;&#10;equation y = x * 2&#13;&#10;solve x&#13;&#10;constraint x >= 0&#13;&#10;end</pre></details>
editor.nod_help.trans.extra=<h2>Esempi trans</h2><p><a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:trans"><code>trans</code></a> traduce un valore completo. Usalo per parole, codici fissi, stati, codici postali e liste brevi.</p><div class="notice"><b>Struttura:</b> <code>trans "old value","new value"</code>. L input completo deve corrispondere al valore a sinistra.</div><details open><summary>Tradurre testo esatto</summary><table><tr><th>Obiettivo</th><th>Regola</th><th>Risultato</th></tr><tr><td>Word</td><td><code>trans "hallo","hello"</code></td><td><code>hallo</code> -> <code>hello</code></td></tr><tr><td>Status</td><td><code>trans "open","in progress"</code></td><td><code>open</code> -> <code>in progress</code></td></tr><tr><td>Address</td><td><code>trans "2566 GB 241","Nieboerweg 241, 2566 GB Den Haag"</code></td><td>postcode + house number -> address</td></tr></table></details><details><summary>trans / chg</summary><table><tr><th>Comando</th><th>Quando</th><th>Esempio</th></tr><tr><td><a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:trans"><code>trans</code></a></td><td>L input completo è conosciuto esattamente.</td><td><code>hallo</code> -> <code>hello</code></td></tr><tr><td><a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:chg"><code>chg</code></a></td><td>Cambia solo l inizio o il pattern.</td><td><code>01751-xxxxx</code> -> <code>070-51xxxxx</code></td></tr></table></details><details><summary>Errori comuni</summary><ul><li>A sinistra c è l input, a destra l output.</li><li>Usa <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:chg"><code>chg</code></a> per cambiamenti parziali.</li><li>Evita traduzioni duplicate per lo stesso input.</li></ul></details>
editor.nod_help.full.classic=<h2>Introduzione editor NOD</h2><p>L editor NOD è lo spazio di lavoro dei convertitori. Scrivi il codice in alto, testi input/output in basso e l anteprima a destra mostra etichette, simboli, testo introduttivo e risultati.</p><h2>Classico 1.73 e NOD 2.0</h2><table><tr><th>Syscalculator 1.73 / NOD 1.0</th><th>Syscalculator 2.0 / editor NOD</th></tr><tr><td>File di testo classici con <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:name"><code>Name</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:input1"><code>input1</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:input2"><code>input2</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:math"><code>math</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:trans"><code>trans</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:chg"><code>chg</code></a> e <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:end"><code>end</code></a>.</td><td>La stessa base rimane compatibile con i vecchi file NOD.</td></tr><tr><td>La posizione dei simboli andava spesso ricordata e testata.</td><td>L anteprima mostra subito <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:symb1"><code>Symb1</code></a> fino a <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:symb4"><code>Symb4</code></a>.</td></tr><tr><td><a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:chg"><code>chg</code></a> era soprattutto sostituzione di prefisso.</td><td><a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:chg"><code>chg</code></a> resta compatibile; NOD 2.0 aggiunge pattern con capture <code>x</code>.</td></tr><tr><td>L aiuto veniva soprattutto dagli esempi.</td><td>L editor offre suggerimenti, aiuto con clic destro e pagine di esempi.</td></tr></table><h2>Sintassi: panoramica completa NOD 1.0 e NOD 2.0</h2><p>Questa tabella mostra quale sintassi viene dai file NOD classici e cosa è stato aggiunto in NOD 2.0.</p><table class="syntax-compare"><tr><th>Syntax / feature</th><th>NOD 1.0</th><th>NOD 2.0</th><th>Note</th></tr><tr><td><a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:name"><code>Name</code></a></td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td>Converter name/title.</td></tr><tr><td><a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:urln"><code>URLN</code></a></td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td>Reference/source line remains supported.</td></tr><tr><td><a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:input1"><code>input1</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:input2"><code>input2</code></a></td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td>Labels for input and output.</td></tr><tr><td><a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:result"><code>Result</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:resfou"><code>Resfou</code></a></td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td>Result label and error text.</td></tr><tr><td><a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:symb1"><code>Symb1</code></a> through <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:symb4"><code>Symb4</code></a></td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td>Symbols left/right of input and output; NOD 2.0 shows them in preview.</td></tr><tr><td><code>format #.00</code></td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td>Number formatting stays the same.</td></tr><tr><td><code>mode calculator</code></td><td><span class="no">×</span></td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td>NOD 2.0 uses <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:mode"><code>mode</code></a> for special file types; normal converters also work without mode.</td></tr><tr><td><code>mode data</code></td><td><span class="no">×</span></td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td>For table/field processing.</td></tr><tr><td><code>mode equation</code></td><td><span class="no">×</span></td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td>For solving equations with <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:given"><code>given</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:equation"><code>equation</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:solve"><code>solve</code></a>.</td></tr><tr><td><code>math ans * 1.8</code></td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td>Classic calculation with <code>ans</code>.</td></tr><tr><td><code>math sqrt(ans^2 + 25)</code></td><td><span class="no">×</span></td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td>Richer formulas and functions in NOD 2.0.</td></tr><tr><td><code>chg "01751-","070-51"</code></td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td>Classic prefix replacement keeps working.</td></tr><tr><td><code>chg "0183x-xx xx","0183-x0 xx xx"</code></td><td><span class="no">×</span></td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td>New in NOD 2.0: pattern with <code>x</code> capture.</td></tr><tr><td><code>trans "old","new"</code></td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td>Exact text translation remains compatible.</td></tr><tr><td><a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:reverse"><code>reverse</code></a></td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td>Reverse direction of a converter.</td></tr><tr><td><a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:table"><code>table</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:field"><code>field</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:output"><code>output</code></a></td><td><span class="no">×</span></td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td>NOD 2.0 data converters with fields and output construction.</td></tr><tr><td><a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:phoneformat"><code>phoneformat</code></a></td><td><span class="no">×</span></td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td>Format phone numbers in data/number converters.</td></tr><tr><td><a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:lookup"><code>lookup</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:match"><code>match</code></a></td><td><span class="no">×</span></td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td>Look up tables or connect values.</td></tr><tr><td><a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:given"><code>given</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:equation"><code>equation</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:solve"><code>solve</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:constraint"><code>constraint</code></a></td><td><span class="no">×</span></td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td>Solve equations with constraints.</td></tr><tr><td><a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:preview"><code>preview</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:backup"><code>backup</code></a></td><td><span class="no">×</span></td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td>Editor/safety information for NOD 2.0 files.</td></tr><tr><td><code>indoprint ... indoend</code></td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td>Introduction text remains supported.</td></tr><tr><td><a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:end"><code>end</code></a></td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td>Closes the NOD file.</td></tr><tr><td>Live preview, suggestions, right-click help</td><td><span class="no">×</span></td><td><span class="yes">✓</span></td><td>This is editor help, not old runtime syntax.</td></tr></table><h2>Cosa resta uguale</h2><ul><li>Comandi leggibili riga per riga.</li><li><a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:end"><code>end</code></a> chiude il file.</li><li>Un convertitore semplice resta breve.</li></ul><h2>Cosa è nuovo</h2><ul><li>Anteprima live e simulatore.</li><li>Graph Preview per grafici dei convertitori math.</li><li>Suggerimenti durante la scrittura.</li><li>Aiuto più ricco per comando.</li><li>Più esempi per <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:math"><code>math</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:trans"><code>trans</code></a>, <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:chg"><code>chg</code></a>, simboli e <a class="cmd-link" href="nodpage:cmd:indoprint"><code>indoprint</code></a>.</li></ul>
editor.nod_help.page.classic=Introduzione editor NOD
